"""The fourteen fixed Journal features, not inferred descriptions of their readers."""
ROWS=[]
def add(person,subject,lines):
    replies=[s.strip() for s in lines.split('|')]
    assert len(replies)==11,(person,len(replies))
    ROWS.append(dict(key='kanto_journal_'+person.lower(),labels=['PokemonJournal_Text_SpecialFeature'+person],subject=subject,replies=replies))
add('Brock','A Journal says Brock seldom laughs but struggles to stop once he starts.',
"I want to hear the joke that gets through his defenses.|An infrequent laugh is not necessarily a small one.|Good. Everyone should have something that gets them laughing.|I like imagining the serious face finally giving up.|The quietest person at dinner can start the biggest laughing fit.|A stern exterior guarding an absolutely catastrophic giggle.|A stone face with a hidden structural weakness.|Now I want to know what reliably triggers it.|Even a mountain can discover it has an echo.|Somebody has definitely made him laugh at the worst possible moment.|That is a side of him I hope his friends get to see.")
add('Misty','A Journal says Misty deeply admires Lorelei.',
"Even a Gym Leader can have someone she hopes to impress.|A respected example can give ambition a useful direction.|Nothing wrong with looking up to someone good.|I wonder if Lorelei knows what her example means to Misty.|It is nice to know even confident people started by admiring someone.|A formidable trainer with a formidable favorite.|A little admiration beneath all that confidence.|Studying someone skilled can help you set concrete goals.|Even a strong current began by finding somewhere to flow.|I hope she gets to tell Lorelei without a magazine doing it first.|I would ask which part of Lorelei's style first caught her attention.")
add('LtSurge','A Journal repeats a rumor that Surge piloted a plane powered by Pokemon electricity.',
"A Pokemon-powered plane? I would spend the whole trip thanking the Pokemon.|I would need more than a rumor before assessing that power system.|Hope the Pokemon got a say in being the engine.|I wonder what that sounded like from the ground.|That is a story I would like to hear over a very long lunch.|An aviation story with an unusually lively power source.|A plane depending on a creature having a sufficiently good day.|I have questions about the regulator. Several questions.|If the story is true, those partners shared quite a sky.|He must get asked about that at every gathering.|I would love to see an actual photograph from that part of his life.")
add('Erika','A Journal repeats a rumor that Erika often naps in the Gym.',
"A little nap among plants sounds extremely easy to understand.|Rest is ordinary. Turning it into a feature is the stranger part.|Let her rest if nothing needs doing.|A quiet room full of leaves would make a lovely place to drift off.|A well-earned nap after lunch can improve everybody's afternoon.|An exclusive report: local woman occasionally becomes tired.|A flower garden with an excellent sleep endorsement.|Comfortable environment confirmed. Productivity conclusions unproven.|A little stillness among growing things is no great mystery.|Peeking at someone asleep is not a hobby I plan to encourage.|I hope people let her have the quiet the place was made for.")
add('Koga','A Journal describes Koga medical knowledge and medicines he prepares for his Pokemon.',
"I like knowing those partners have someone who knows how to help them.|Knowing how to treat harm matters alongside knowing how to inflict it.|A strong trainer should know how to care for the team afterward.|That is a quieter kind of skill than the Gym shows off.|Making something that helps a partner recover takes patient care.|The poison specialist also knows the restorative chapter.|A useful reminder that dangerous knowledge can have gentle work to do.|I would ask how he checks the preparations are safe.|The same careful hands can tend what they know could be hurt.|That deserves as much attention as the intimidating reputation.|I would rather hear about a partner recovering than another frightening trick.")
add('Sabrina','A Journal says Sabrina can communicate with her Pokemon in battle without speaking.',
"I would still say thank you out loud. It feels nice to hear.|The report describes silent coordination. The mechanism remains worth asking about.|If the team understands, the orders do not need an audience.|I wonder whether it feels like a voice or something without words.|I hope there is still room for an ordinary comforting word afterward.|A commanding performance with no lines for the audience to quote.|An entire conversation the room is not invited to hear.|An unusually direct communication channel, if the account is accurate.|Some understanding may arrive before a word can put on its coat.|People already assume I should know what they mean. She might actually manage.|I would like to know what the Pokemon notice first when she reaches out.")
add('Blaine','A Journal claims Blaine removes his shades when devising quiz questions.',
"The glasses come off. Somewhere, a perfectly innocent question becomes a trap.|I doubt the eyewear is necessary, but rituals can help concentration.|The important part is whether the question makes sense.|Maybe that is how people know to leave him to his thoughts.|Everyone has a small habit when thinking through something difficult.|The shades are apparently the curtain between us and another quiz.|A warning signal for the approach of organized trivia.|I want to test whether he writes better questions without them.|A little uncovered gaze, searching for something else to ask.|Someone noticed that often enough to make it his public fact.|I wonder whether he knows people have identified his thinking face.")
add('Lorelei','A Journal praises Lorelei calculated battling and teases an unspecified surprising secret.',
"They cannot just say secret and leave the page looking that pleased.|The battle description is useful. The unspecified secret is a sales device.|If she wants to keep something private, let her.|I would rather hear what she enjoys when she chooses to tell us.|We know she can battle. We do not need every other part of her life.|A magnificent little hook with no fish attached.|An entire paragraph trying to sell us an unopened drawer.|Precise battling described precisely. Then the article gives up on precision.|Some doors belong to the person who closes them.|Being impressive in public does not make her private life a prize.|I would prefer a question she wants to answer to a secret someone wants to expose.")
add('Bruno','A Journal attributes Bruno joining the Elite Four to his desire to battle the strongest trainers.',
"He found a job where the difficult part is exactly what he wanted.|A demanding position aligned with a clear personal ambition.|He wanted strong opponents. He put himself where they would arrive.|It must feel good to reach a place you worked toward.|That kind of work takes more than wanting it on one determined morning.|An ambition with the courage to choose a very inconvenient workplace.|He built a life in the path of very formidable visitors.|Clear objective. Extremely demanding implementation.|A strong wish can become the place where someone stands.|I hope he has something he enjoys on the days nobody challenges him.|I would ask what the best battle taught him, rather than just who won.")
add('Agatha','A Journal reports that Agatha and Oak were rival trainers when young.',
"Those two used to challenge each other? That must have been a lively route.|Their shared history predates the roles we know them for.|Old rivals tend to remember things no title can erase.|I wonder if either still remembers one particular match perfectly.|I can imagine a very competitive conversation over tea.|Two impressive careers with an old argument tucked into the roots.|A rivalry old enough to have collected its own ghosts.|Competition may have helped shape both of them.|Long years do not always quiet a familiar challenge.|She probably knows stories that would make his students sit very still.|I would love to see a photograph from a day they still thought everything was ahead.")
add('Lance','A Journal suggests Lance grandfather is an elder of a renowned dragon-master clan.',
"Imagine bringing home your first Pokemon when the family specializes in dragons.|A possible family tradition, though the article leaves the relationship tentative.|His family may have taught him plenty. He still had to do the work.|That sounds like a childhood with some very large expectations.|Family knowledge can be a gift. It can also arrive with instructions nobody asked for.|A family tree with an unusually high chance of breathing fire.|An impressive inheritance, with teeth attached.|I would ask what practical knowledge was passed down.|Some families carry their old stories on very large wings.|I hope he got to choose what part of the family story became his.|I wonder which small lesson from his grandfather he still uses.")
add('ProfOak','A Journal reports Oak lives with his grandchildren Daisy and the rival.',
"A busy household, a busy lab. I hope someone reminds him to eat.|Living arrangements are a small part of a life. The article gives us only that part.|Being somebody's grandfather matters alongside the famous job.|It is strange to read a familiar family detail in a feature.|I wonder who notices first when everyone has missed lunch.|The celebrated professor also has ordinary household negotiations.|A grand public name, with a very ordinary front door.|I hope the household gets more quiet than the lab.|Even a well-known life has a place where the kettle needs filling.|Imagine your home situation becoming a magazine paragraph.|I would rather hear a family story they chose to share than keep inspecting the address.")
add('DaisyOak','An old Journal names Daisy Oak as the Spring Contest Grand Champion.',
"Daisy won the whole spring Contest? I hope someone cheered themselves hoarse.|That is a documented achievement, not simply a flattering description.|Good for her. That would have taken real preparation.|I wish we could have heard the room when her name was called.|I hope the celebration afterward was as warm as the victory.|A champion's chapter, quietly waiting on an old shelf.|A familiar name carrying a bright season behind it.|An award like that represents a lot of work people did not see.|A spring preserved between pages, with her name at its center.|I would absolutely ask about the outfit and then the entire performance.|I wonder which moment from that day she most likes remembering.")
add('MrFuji','A Journal notes Fuji declined an interview and describes the community respect for him.',
"He said no, and they still found something kind to print. Good.|Declining an interview does not diminish the care people observe in his work.|He does not owe a magazine his story.|I like that his kindness reached people without him having to explain it.|Some people show you who they are by what they do each day.|A man who declined the spotlight and remained visible through his kindness.|A quiet refusal, surrounded by a town's affection.|Observable care is a stronger account than a forced interview.|He can leave a page blank and still be known gently.|I am glad they printed the refusal without treating it like a scandal.|I would rather notice how the Pokemon settle near him than make him pose.")
